  "summary": "The paper studies CL-QAS, a gate-based variational quantum architecture search method with tensor-train amplitude encoding, on 20-qubit IBM Heron r2 hardware for two tasks: ECG classification and financial time-series forecasting. Reported hardware results are modest but consistent: ECG achieves Acc 0.863, bAcc 0.900, F1 0.496, and financial forecasting achieves Acc 0.607, bAcc 0.607, F1 0.624; no practical quantum advantage over classical methods is demonstrated.",
